Suppose I am running a program in C. I have a struct with four fields, first-name, last-name, address, and telephone. I do not want to print the entire struct, but only fields that I know what to print. For example, I want to print the first, last, and telephone fields of the struct. What is the best way to do this?

I understand that the general way to write such code is:

```
void test_program(struct person p)
{
    printf("First name: %s\n", (char*)p->first_name);
    printf("Last name:  %s\n", (char*)p->last_name);
    printf("Address:    %s\n", (char*)p->address);
    printf("Telephone:  %s\n", (char*)p->telephone);
}

```

I would like to know if there is a more efficient, if not more concise, way.

Thanks a lot.
You could use a [`struct()`](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Struct_%28programming%29) member function (`print_field`):

```
void test_program(struct person p)
{
    printf("First name: %s\n", (char*)p->first_name);
    printf("Last name: %s\n", (char*)p->last_name);
}

```
